<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Helvis of Ramla</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Helvis of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ramla">Ramla</a> was the heiress of the lordship of Ramla in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-jerusalem">Kingdom of Jerusalem</a>, daughter of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baldwin-of-ibelin">Baldwin of Ramla</a>. Her marriage to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/barisan-of-ibelin">Barisan of Ibelin</a> brought Ramla to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-ibelin">Ibelin family</a>, and their sons Hugh, Baldwin and Balian became leading barons of the kingdom. After Barisan's death in 1150 she married Manasses of Hierges, constable of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jerusalem">Jerusalem</a>.</p></div>
